  "finalText": "Both issues were real, and I've fixed them.\n\n**Issue 1: T-2015 and T-2016 were never triaged.** I had only read page 1 of the listing. I checked that neither is a duplicate or a security report.\n- **T-2015 (payroll, department impact, Finance payslips missing):**\n  - Set to sev1, the matrix value.\n  - Due 09:10 today, which is 08:10 triage plus the 60-minute sev1 target on the clock.\n  - Assigned to E-201, the business-apps engineer on call at 09:10 (not on leave).\n  - I did not escalate it to incident-command, because only company-wide outages are major incidents. The handbook also keeps a ticket inside its owning rotation. I paged no one.\n- **T-2016 (VPN, single-user, token app asks to register again):**\n  - Set to sev4, the matrix value.\n  - Due Thu 2026-03-26 17:00, counting 1440 business minutes from the 09:00 opening and skipping the 25 March holiday.\n  - Assigned to E-302, the network-primary engineer on call at that moment (not on leave).\n  - It reads as a token-registration problem, not phishing.\n\n**Issue 2: T-1999 was the same problem as T-2003.** Both are the Payments pipeline failing since Saturday night.\n- T-2003 was created 3/21 22:30 and T-1999 on 3/23 06:30, so T-2003 stays as the survivor.\n- T-1999 carried a committed deadline of 10:30, earlier than T-2003's 12:10. I merged T-1999 into T-2003 and set T-2003's deadline to 10:30.\n- I re-read both tickets afterwards. T-2003 is open, assigned to E-101, due 10:30. T-1999 shows as merged into T-2003.\n\n**Issue 3: verification.** I re-read T-2003 and T-1999 after the changes. I did not re-read T-2015 or T-2016; the tool output confirmed each change. I left the rest of the earlier work alone, since the verifier confirmed it was correct.",
